    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) stands out as our premier option. His matchup against Nick Martinez is exceptionally favorable, as the combination of a high-xERA opponent and a boost from the hitter-friendly park environment allows **Lawrence Butler** to capitalize on his elite platoon profile. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.47) also anchor the top of our lineup today; **Jung Hoo Lee** gains significant utility from his projected leadoff spot and a strong wind-out advantage, while **Jonathan Aranda** is positioned to maximize his output against Mason Barnett. Both **Bryce Harper** (65.00) and **Yainer Diaz** (63.62) provide high-floor stability, with **Bryce Harper** maintaining strong xwOBA indicators even against a moderate matchup.\n\nWe are navigating a few situational risks, most notably for **Cal Raleigh** (54.46), whose score is dampened by a 31% rain risk and a difficult encounter with Weathers. Meanwhile, our most difficult decision involved **Gleyber Torres** (53.06) and **Justin Crawford** (52.68). **Gleyber Torres** was the final cut from the active roster; despite his favorable order position, his dynamic platoon splits against Tanner Bibee were neutralized by the SP's skill, ultimately pushing him below the efficiency threshold of our starters like **Daulton Varsho** and **Braden Montgomery**. We also remain cautious of **Jeremiah Jackson** (61.47); while he offers marginal SB upside due to a slow pitcher delivery, the low order placement limits his overall run-scoring potential. We continue to monitor the lineups for **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Zack Gelof**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Kyle Karros** to ensure these projections hold as the official cards are posted.",
